H1 one client writes, then reads its write
    C1 write 1  [0, 2]
    C1 read -> 1  [3, 4]
  linearizable:            yes, e.g. C1:w1 C1:r1
  sequentially consistent: yes, e.g. C1:w1 C1:r1

H2 a read overlaps a write and sees the old value; a later read sees the new one
    C1 write 1  [0, 10]
    C2 read -> 0  [2, 4]
    C2 read -> 1  [6, 8]
  linearizable:            yes, e.g. C2:r0 C1:w1 C2:r1
  sequentially consistent: yes, e.g. C2:r0 C1:w1 C2:r1

H3 stale read: the write finished before the read started, yet the read returns 0
    C1 write 1  [0, 5]
    C2 read -> 0  [6, 8]
  linearizable:            no
  sequentially consistent: yes, e.g. C2:r0 C1:w1

H4 new then old: C2 sees the new value, later C3 sees the old one
    C1 write 1  [0, 10]
    C2 read -> 1  [2, 4]
    C3 read -> 0  [6, 8]
  linearizable:            no
  sequentially consistent: yes, e.g. C3:r0 C1:w1 C2:r1

H5 C2 sees the two writes of C1 in the wrong order
    C1 write 1  [0, 2]
    C1 write 2  [3, 5]
    C2 read -> 2  [6, 7]
    C2 read -> 1  [8, 9]
  linearizable:            no
  sequentially consistent: no

H6 a client does not see its own write
    C1 write 5  [0, 2]
    C1 read -> 0  [3, 4]
  linearizable:            no
  sequentially consistent: no

